"1315184500010891","Centrafrique : La ville de Bouar célèbre la 15 ème édition de la Foire Agro-pastorale.
La Première Dame de Centrafrique Tina Marguerite TOUADERA a mis le cap à Bouar dans la préfecture de la Nana Mambéré pour lancer la 15 ème édition de la foire Agro-pastorale. Organisée par l'Organisation Nationale des Femmes Rurales de la ville de Bouar, avec l'appui technique et stratégique de la Fédération des Associations des Femmes Entrepreneurs de Centrafrique (FAFECA), cet événement à regrouper plus de 500  femmes venues des localités différentes. Les autorités locales et administratives ont accompagné la Première Dame dans sa mission pour encourager et féliciter les agricultrices de travailler davantage, car la terre ne ment jamais.","French","politics","domestic politics","not foreign politics","not resource distribution","not applicable","not applicable","not applicable","not applicable","not applicable","not applicable","no mention of the US","no mention of the Russia","no mention of the China","no mention of the UN","no mention of the IMF","no mention of democracy","not anti-western","no mention of the nation or national unity","no mention of specific subgroup","not applicable","no mention of africa","no mention of political opponents","no mention of religion","no mention of violent group","NOT CODED","AGRICULTURE;CIVIL RIGHTS;CULTURE"
"1061580225992938","15th February 2025 - Today marks the conclusion of the National Women Conference, organized by the National Ministry of Gender, under the theme ""Strengthening Women's Structures for Gender Equality"".

I'm deeply honored to have been a part of this historic conference, which brought together women delegates from all ten states and the three administrative areas. The energy, passion, and dedication to gender equality were really visible throughout the event.

The conference achieved its goal of electing a new office of the South Sudan Women Union (formerly South Sudan Women General Association). During the five days, delegates thoroughly reviewed the constitution, elected the new executive and council offices, and paved the way for a brighter future.

The conference was opened on 11th February by H.E. Mama Rebecca Nyandeng de Mabior, Vice President and Chair of the Gender and Youth Cluster.  On the 4th day, 14th February, of the conference, the event was graced by H.E. Josephine Joseph Lagu, Vice President and Chair of the Services Cluster. Other leaders who attended were Rt. Hon. Jemma Nunu Kumba, Speaker of the National Assembly, Rt. Hon. Mary Ayen Mijok, 1st Deputy Speaker of the Councol of States, National Ministers, MPs from the two assemblies, states’ Ministers of Gender and their delegates, civil society, faith based groups, women in the organized forces, and all women from different walks of life and from various institutions.

This milestone marks a significant step forward for us, the women of South Sudan, as we unite to develop a way forward together. The success of this event is just the beginning – the real work lies ahead, and I'm excited to see the impact that we women will make.

Thanks to the National Ministry of Gender for organizing this groundbreaking conference!","English","politics","domestic politics","not foreign politics","not resource distribution","not applicable","not applicable","not applicable","not applicable","not applicable","not applicable","no mention of the US","no mention of the Russia","no mention of the China","no mention of the UN","no mention of the IMF","positive towards democracy","not anti-western","national unity","no mention of specific subgroup","not applicable","no mention of africa","no mention of political opponents","no mention of religion","no mention of violent group","NOT CODED","CIVIL RIGHTS;GOVERNMENT OPERATIONS"
