"2.17758E+15","Marhai Forest Reserve Becomes a National Park

The Nasarawa State Government has officially handed over the Marhai Forest Reserve to the Federal Government, marking a milestone in biodiversity conservation.

At the handover in Lafia, the Minister of Federal Ministry of Environment Balarabe Abbas Lawal, commended Governor Abdullahi Sule and the people of Nasarawa for their environmental commitment. He highlighted the ecological and economic importance of the reserve, home to diverse wildlife and the iconic Farin Ruwa Waterfalls, with potential to boost ecotourism and local livelihoods.

The Federal Government plans to ensure community involvement, enhance ranger security, and partner with local and international stakeholders to manage the park sustainably.

This collaboration sets a precedent for environmental stewardship in Nigeria, preserving natural heritage for future generations.","English","politics","domestic politics","foreign politics","not resource distribution","not applicable","not applicable","not applicable","not applicable","not applicable","mentions sustainability","no mention of the US","no mention of the Russia","no mention of the China","no mention of the UN","no mention of the IMF","no mention of democracy","not anti-western","no mention of the nation or national unity","subgroup unity","people of Nasarawa ","no mention of africa","no mention of political opponents","no mention of religion","no mention of violent group","NOT CODED","ENVIRONMENT;PUBLIC LANDS;GOVERNMENT OPERATIONS"
