"1526638302111706","#EBS2024 The National Department of Health (South Africa) in collaboration with Africa CDC, WHO South Africa and RISE (USAID programme for Epidemic Control) convened an event-based surveillance (EBS) workshop in Boksburg. The 5-day workshop was attended by public health experts and officials responsible for health emergency surveillance, detection and reporting, as well as response. It was held to adapt the national guidelines for the Event-Based Surveillance (EBS). This will enhance the surveillance of public health threats across various sectors, ensuring early detection, reporting and responding to the health emergencies.

