"1922120352076647","The Ministry of Health’s three-day sensitization workshop on drug and substance abuse in Kakamega County culminated in a public baraza on February 20, 2025.

The event brought together stakeholders from the National Government, County Governments, organizations involved in drug and substance abuse control, and members of the public from the Western region.

Discussions focused on raising awareness about the dangers of drug and substance abuse, with particular emphasis on the increasing use of novel tobacco and nicotine products.

Statistics presented during the forum highlighted high levels of marijuana and chang’aa abuse in the region, underscoring the urgent need for stronger enforcement, community engagement, and policy interventions.

