"4357485257812968","AfDB Applauds Delta Automotive Technology for Global Impact and Youth Empowerment

The African Development Bank’s Deputy Director General for Southern Africa, Moono Mupotola, has praised Delta Automotive Technology Company for its remarkable growth and dominance in the global automotive industry.

Speaking during a visit to the company’s facilities in Lobatse, Mupotola said Delta Automotive Technology is a shining example of value for money, having been funded through the Botswana Development Corporation with support from the African Development Bank. She commended the company not only for its impressive market performance but also for its significant role in creating employment for young Batswana, especially young women.

Delta Automotive Technology CEO revealed that the company received a P100 million funding package when it was established in 2015 after relocating from South Africa. Today, it boasts a workforce of 365 employees—95% of whom are Batswana, with women making up 75% of the team.

He explained that the company specializes in the production and supply of electronic components for global automotive giants such as Volkswagen (VW) and Nissan, serving both the European and Asian markets. On average, Delta Automotive Technology exports 120 electronic components daily.

Mupotola’s visit to Lobatse was part of her tour to engage with and appreciate projects funded by the African Development Bank across Southern Africa.","English","politics","domestic politics","foreign politics","resource distribution","national government","specific locality or group","not applicable","Lobatse","resources for women","not applicable","no mention of the US","no mention of the Russia","no mention of the China","no mention of the UN","no mention of the IMF","no mention of democracy","not anti-western","no mention of the nation or national unity","no mention of specific subgroup","not applicable","african unity","no mention of political opponents","no mention of religion","no mention of violent group","NOT CODED","DOMESTIC COMMERCE;LABOR;INTERNATIONAL AFFAIRS"
