"1272678720410694","Ministry of Planning and Development Holds Workshop on Draft Climate-Smart Public Investment Management Regulations
*******************************************************************************************************
The Ministry of Planning and Development of Ethiopia, in collaboration with the World Bank, hosted a stakeholder consultation workshop on the draft Climate Change Public Investment Management (PIM) Regulations and Guidelines. H.E Bereket Fesehatsion, State Minister of the Ministry of Planning and Development, delivered the opening remarks, underscoring the importance of addressing climate change.
A total of 50 participants from various agencies, including the Ministry of Finance, Ministry of Agriculture, Ministry of Water and Energy, Ministry of Transport, Ethiopian Environmental Protection Authority, Ethiopia Biodiversity Institute, Ministry of Urban Development and Infrastructure, and Ministry of Irrigation and Lowland, joined the workshop, representing key stakeholders in the development process.
H.E. Bereket highlighted the Ministry's efforts, alongside the World Bank and other stakeholders, to enhance Ethiopia’s PIM system. These efforts aim to tackle challenges such as cost overruns, delays, and quality issues, which have arisen from unclear legal frameworks defining roles in the PIM process. The Federal Public Project Management and Administration Proclamation No. 1210/2012 and its six subsidiary guidelines have shown promising results in addressing these challenges.
However, H.E. Bereket noted that climate change has not yet been fully integrated into Ethiopia's PIM system. To address this gap, the Ministry is actively working to incorporate climate change considerations into the country's development policies and public investments. He emphasized that such integration would bolster the resilience, sustainability, and greenness of Ethiopia's economic development while supporting its commitments to global climate goals.
To facilitate this integration, an appropriate legal framework is essential. While the Ethiopian government has made significant strides in demonstrating its commitment to climate action, H.E. Bereket stressed the need for concrete actions on the ground. The draft Climate Change PIM Regulations and Guidelines represent a practical commitment by the government to address climate change, particularly at the project level.
H.E. Bereket encouraged all participants to engage actively in discussions, as collaboration among stakeholders is crucial for effective, efficient, and sustainable socio-economic development.
The workshop featured presentations on global best practices for integrating climate change into development agendas. Following these presentations, participants provided relevant feedback and clarifications on the draft regulations and guidelines. A constructive dialogue ensued, leading to a broader consensus on the agendas discussed. Participants also agreed on the necessary follow-up steps to ensure the workshop's outcomes are effectively implemented.
In closing of the Workshop, Mr. Tegene Hailu, CEO of the Plan and Public Investment Management Division, summarized Ethiopia's progress in strengthening its PIM system. He acknowledged the ongoing challenge of integrating climate change with the development agenda and reiterated the workshop's goal to tackle this issue. The Ministry of Planning and Development will continue to engage stakeholders until the regulations are approved by the Council of Ministers.","English","politics","domestic politics","foreign politics","not resource distribution","not applicable","not applicable","not applicable","not applicable","not applicable","mentions climate change","no mention of the US","no mention of the Russia","no mention of the China","no mention of the UN","no mention of the IMF","no mention of democracy","not anti-western","no mention of the nation or national unity","no mention of specific subgroup","not applicable","no mention of africa","no mention of political opponents","no mention of religion","no mention of violent group","NOT CODED","ENVIRONMENT;GOVERNMENT OPERATIONS;ECONOMY"
"1612859606765228","በፕላንና ልማት ሚኒስትር ዶ/ር ፍፁም አሰፋ  የተመራው የፌዴራል የሱፐርቪዥን ቡድን በአቃቂ ቃሊቲ ክ/ከተማ የሚገኙ ሰው ተኮር ስራዎችንና የአገልግሎት አሰጣጥን ተዘዋውሮ ተመልክቷል፡፡
-------------------------------------------------------------------
የኢኖቬሽንና ቴክኖሎጂ ሚኒስቴር ሚኒስትር ዶ/ር በለጠ ሞላ  ጨምሮ ሌሎች የፌዴራል ከፍተኛ የሥራ ኃላፊዎችን ያካተተው የሱፐርቪዥን ቡድን በአቃቂ ቃሊቲ ክ/ከተማ  የሚገኙ የተለያዩ ሰው ተኮር የልማት ፕሮጀክቶች፣የተፈጠሩ ምቹ የስራ ቦታዎች፣ የሌማት ትሩፋት እና ስራ ዕድል ፈጠራ ስራዎች እና ተኪ ምርት አምራች ኢንዱስትሪዎችን ተዟዙሮ ምልከታ አካሂዷል።
በተለያዩ ማህበራዊ እና ኢኮኖሚያዊ ቀውስ ውስጥ የሚገኙ ሴቶችን የተለያዩ ሞያዊ ስልጠናዎችን በመስጠት ራሳቸውን እንዲችሉ ለማድረግ የተቋቋመውን የነገዋ የሴቶች የተሀድሶና የክህሎት ማበልፀጊያ ማዕከል ፣ ከመላው የሀገሪቱ ክፍል የተውጣጡ ዓይነ ስውራን ተማሪዎች የሚማሩበት በአይነቱ ልዩ የሆነው  ክብርት ሼይካ ፋጢማ ቢንት ሙባረክ የአይነ ስውራን አዳሪ ት/ቤት ፣ 
በከተማው የሚስተዋለውን የዋጋ ንረትና የምርት አቅርቦት እንዳይከሰት አጋዥ የሆኑ በወረዳ 08 እና በወረዳ 09 እየተከናወኑ የሚገኘውን የተቀናጀ የከተማ ግብርና ስራዎች፣ የመኸር መሰብሰብ እና የበጋ የግብርና ስራ የማስጀመር ስራ የተሰራ ሲሆን፣በክ/ከተማው ለሚገኙ ከ600 በላይ ለሚሆኑ ስራ አጥ ነዋሪዎች የስራ እድል የፈጠረና ተኪ ምርቶችን እያመረተ የሚገኘውን ሌጀንድ ጨርቃ ጨርቅ ፋብሪካ በክፍለ ከተማው ከተሰሩት መካከል ናቸው፡፡
አቃቂ ቃሊቲ  የነገዋ የሴቶች የልህቀትና የተሀድሶ ማዕከል ፣ የአይነስውራን አዳሪ ት/ቤት እና ሌሎች ግዙፍ ሰው ተኮር ፕሮጀክቶች ያሉበት ክ /ከተማ ነው ያሉት ዶ/ር ፍፁም አሰፋ ""ልብንም ጭንቅላትንም ለሰዎች ሀሳብ ክፍት ማድረግ እና የቡድን ስራን ማዳበር ለውጤታማነት ወሳኝ ነው!!"" ሲሉ ገልፀዋል፡፡
በክ/ከተማው እየተከናወኑ የሚገኙ ሰው ተኮር የልማት ስራዎች እንደ ሀገር የተያዙ እቅዶችን ከማሳካት አኳያ በርካታ ስራዎች እየተሰሩ መሆኑንና ተስፋ የሚሰጡ ውጤቶች መልከት እንደተቻለ ገልፀው በምልከታው የታዩ ዉጤቶችን ማስፋት እንደሚገባ የሱፐርቪዥን ቡድኑ አባላት ተናግረዋል ።","Other(Amharic)","politics","domestic politics","not foreign politics","resource distribution","national government","specific locality or group","not applicable","Akaki Kality Sub-City; Woreda 08; Woreda 09","resources for women","not applicable","no mention of the US","no mention of the Russia","no mention of the China","no mention of the UN","no mention of the IMF","no mention of democracy","not anti-western","no mention of the nation or national unity","subgroup unity","Akaki Kaliti; Woreda 08 and Woreda 09,","no mention of africa","no mention of political opponents","no mention of religion","no mention of violent group","NOT CODED","LABOR;SOCIAL WELFARE;AGRICULTURE"
