"1951960715588303","ZAMBIA EVENING WEATHER FORECAST: WEDNESDAY (25/12/2024)
SUMMARY:
A relatively moist airflow from the northeast is influencing the weather over most parts of Zambia resulting in partly cloudy and hot weather with isolated rainfall activities.

FORECAST FOR TONIGHT: WEDNESDAY (25/12/2024)
Southern, Western, Northwestern, Copperbelt, Luapula, Eastern, Central and Lusaka Provinces including the western parts of Northern province:
Partly cloudy, windy at times and mild with isolated rain and occasional thunder. 
Muchinga Province including the eastern parts of Northern provinces:* Few clouds, windy at times and warm to mild.           

FORECAST FOR TOMORROW: THURSDAY (26/12/2024)
Southern, Western, Northwestern, Copperbelt, Luapula, Central and Lusaka Provinces including the western parts of Northern and Eastern provinces: 
Morning: Partly cloudy, windy at times and mild to warm becoming mainly cloudy by late morning with isolated rainfall. Minimum temperature will range between 15°C and 22°C.
Afternoon: Mainly cloudy, slightly windy and warm to hot with isolated showers and thundershowers. Maximum temperature will range between 29°C and 36°C.  
Evening: Partly cloudy, slightly windy and warm to mild with isolated rain and occasional thunder. 
Muchinga Province including the eastern parts of Northern and Eastern provinces:
Morning: Partly cloudy, slightly windy and mild to warm with a chance of isolated rainfall. Minimum temperature will range between 16°C and 23°C.
Afternoon: Partly cloudy, slightly windy and hot to very hot with a chance of showers. Maximum temperature will range between 33°C and 39C.  
Evening:Partly cloudy, slightly windy and warm to mild with a chance of rain.

OUTLOOK TO FRIDAY (27/12/2024)
Partly cloudy conditions to continue over most parts of Zambia with more rains confined to the western half of the Country.

Produced by the Zambia Meteorological Department,

