"871948487764844","This morning, I hosted a United Nations delegation led by Dr. Stephen, the UN Resident Coordinator in Kenya, to discuss our green transition goals focusing on People and Peace as well as Planet and Posterity. We emphasized implementing the Nairobi African Leaders Declaration on Climate Change, aligning our Ministry's strategic plan with the Kenya Kwanza administration's Bottom-up Economic Transformation Agenda.

Together with Principal Secretaries Dr. Eng. Festus Ng'eno and Mr. Gitonga Mugambi, as well as a number of Leadership of UN agencies , we explored climate financing through Kenya's emerging carbon markets. In an effort to benefit the community and support the country’s food and nutritional security needs, we have decided that 30% of the trees from the 15 Billion National Tree Growing Programme will be fruit and fodder species.

Additionally, we discussed sustainable water management project to enhance water access and community resilience against climate change. Policies such as the National Disaster Management Bill and shifts in waste management to a circular economy were highlighted. I underscored our commitment to global collaboration on climate issues, with key attendees including DG NEMA Mamo B. Mamo and others.","English","politics","domestic politics","foreign politics","resource distribution","national government","country-wide","not applicable","not applicable","resources not specifically for women","mentions climate change","no mention of the US","no mention of the Russia","no mention of the China","positive towards the UN","no mention of the IMF","no mention of democracy","not anti-western","national unity","no mention of specific subgroup","not applicable","african unity","no mention of political opponents","no mention of religion","no mention of violent group","NOT CODED","ENVIRONMENT;INTERNATIONAL AFFAIRS;AGRICULTURE"
