"1286699086078959","Presided over the launch of the National Framework for Climate Services and the State of the Climate Kenya Report 2024, a milestone in Kenya's journey toward resilience and sustainability.

This framework equips every sector with timely, reliable and actionable climate data, enhancing our ability to forecast, prepare for and respond to climate variability and extreme events. 

I emphasized the power of science, innovation and partnerships in driving sustainable solutions and called on all stakeholders to join in building a climate-resilient nation.

I was joined by Principal Secretaries Dr. Eng. Festus Ng’eno (Environment and Climate Change), Mr. Gitonga Mugambi (Forestry), Hon. Jonathan Mueke (Livestock Development) and Dr. David Gikungu (KMD Director). Also present was Dr. Fatuma Adan (IGAD Head of Missions).","English","politics","domestic politics","foreign politics","resource distribution","national government","country-wide","not applicable","not applicable","resources not specifically for women","mentions climate change","no mention of the US","no mention of the Russia","no mention of the China","no mention of the UN","no mention of the IMF","no mention of democracy","not anti-western","national unity","no mention of specific subgroup","not applicable","no mention of africa","no mention of political opponents","no mention of religion","no mention of violent group","NOT CODED","ENVIRONMENT;TECHNOLOGY;INTERNATIONAL AFFAIRS"
"1343322150530664","Appeared before the Senate Standing Committee on Delegated Legislation, chaired by Hon. Mwenda Gataya, Senator for Tharaka Nithi, at Bunge Towers, Nairobi.

The session provided an opportunity to brief the committee on the Digital Health Regulations 2025, currently at its prepublication stage. 

These regulations are designed to establish a secure, efficient and patient-centered digital health ecosystem, reinforcing the government's commitment to leveraging technology for Universal Health Coverage (UHC).

A key pillar of these regulations is their role in supporting the implementation of Taifa Care by enhancing data-driven decision-making, streamlining patient records and ensuring seamless interoperability across healthcare facilities. 

I was accompanied by the Acting CEO of the Digital Health Agency (DHA), Mr. Anthony Lenaiyara and senior Ministry officials.","English","politics","domestic politics","not foreign politics","resource distribution","national government","country-wide","not applicable","not applicable","resources not specifically for women","not applicable","no mention of the US","no mention of the Russia","no mention of the China","no mention of the UN","no mention of the IMF","no mention of democracy","not anti-western","no mention of the nation or national unity","no mention of specific subgroup","not applicable","no mention of africa","no mention of political opponents","no mention of religion","no mention of violent group","NOT CODED","HEALTH;TECHNOLOGY;GOVERNMENT OPERATIONS"
"1530025370936429","🇩🇯 🇪🇺 Aujourd’hui, j'ai eu l'honneur de recevoir Mme Sylvie Tabesse, Ambassadrice de l'Union Européenne à Djibouti et auprès de l'IGAD, pour sa visite d’adieu. 

