"1098805702418245","On Monday, I had an audience with delegates from Plan International Germany Foundation, Trust Foundation, and Austria Foundation who are in the country inspecting the projects that they support which <redacted_mention> and other agencies are implementing in various districts across the country.  I was so happy to welcome them at Kamuzu Palace. During this meeting, we discussed a number of issues surrounding girl child education, achievements and plans ahead. 

I am proud of the transformative work being done through the Girls Education for Empowerment (GEE) project—a four-year initiative implemented by Plan International Malawi, which my organization, Shaping Our Future Foundation (SOFF) is a key implementing partner.  

This project supports a total of 730 students, 559 girls and 171 boys with bursaries in public secondary schools across the country. Since its inception on 15 November 2022, the GEE project has worked tirelessly to empower vulnerable children, especially girls, to access, remain in and complete secondary education, and to transition into tertiary education.  

This generosity is not counted in any currency; it is measured in lives changed, in dreams restored, and in doors of opportunity opened wide. Because of our partnership, thousands of girls are now able to sit in classrooms, not as spectators of a world beyond their reach, but as full participants, ready to shape their future. 

I am proud to report that 25 students from the first cohort and 48 from the second cohort under SOFF Bursary Program have made it into public universities. 34 of these students, which represents 47%, were directly supported under the Girls Education for Empowerment Project. 

These brilliant young minds now walk the corridors of institutions of higher learning—a dream that once seemed distant, if not impossible.

Plan International and all our partners are part of this success story.  My desire is to see every girl child in Malawi get a chance to quality education.

Together we can make a difference.","English","politics","domestic politics","foreign politics","resource distribution","international organisations","country-wide","not applicable","not applicable","resources for women","not applicable","no mention of the US","no mention of the Russia","no mention of the China","no mention of the UN","no mention of the IMF","no mention of democracy","not anti-western","national unity","no mention of specific subgroup","not applicable","no mention of africa","no mention of political opponents","no mention of religion","no mention of violent group","NOT CODED","EDUCATION;INTERNATIONAL AFFAIRS"
