"1415799169524722","For Immediate Release

President Boakai Embarks on Two-Day Visit to Accra, Ghana

December 28, 2024 

Executive Mansion, Monrovia – President Joseph Nyuma Boakai, Sr., today, December 28, 2024, embarks on a two-day visit to Accra, Ghana, where he will hold consultations with his Colleagues, the outgoing as well as the incoming Presidents of Ghana, Excellencies Nana Addo Dankwa Akufo-Addo and John Dramani Mahama.

During his visit, the President will honor an invitation to attend the wedding ceremony of the Daughter of a longstanding friend of his.

This visit underscores the strong bond of friendship and cooperation between Liberia and Ghana and reaffirms the President’s commitment to fostering regional solidarity and collaboration.

Honorable Samuel Kofi Woods, National Security Advisor will accompany the President. 

While the President is away from the country, the Honorable Counselor Oswald N. Tweh, Minister of Justice, will preside over the Cabinet while remaining in contact with the Vice President and in consultation with the President.

The President returns to the Capital on Monday, December 30, 2024.","English","politics","domestic politics","foreign politics","not resource distribution","not applicable","not applicable","not applicable","not applicable","not applicable","not applicable","no mention of the US","no mention of the Russia","no mention of the China","no mention of the UN","no mention of the IMF","no mention of democracy","not anti-western","no mention of the nation or national unity","no mention of specific subgroup","not applicable","no mention of africa","no mention of political opponents","no mention of religion","no mention of violent group","NOT CODED","INTERNATIONAL AFFAIRS;GOVERNMENT OPERATIONS"
