"1.11138E+15","We were deeply honored to officiate the handover ceremony of the School Health Project at Malama School in Kasama, marking its place among 595 similar facilities across the country.

The School Health Program is a comprehensive initiative that integrates education and healthcare within a single institution, catering to both the academic and health needs of pupils and their surrounding communities.

We are pleased to note that, so far, 5,000 teachers have been trained as the first line of defense in school health, while 1.5 million learners across 700 schools in all 10 provinces have benefitted from this initiative.

Achieving universal health coverage remains a national priority. These school health facilities and trained health teachers serve as critical entry points for healthcare, playing a vital role in enhancing learners’ well-being, academic performance, and overall development.

We extend our heartfelt congratulations to the Ministries of Education and Health, along with all stakeholders, for their collaborative efforts and their dedication to empowering our learners and being agents of positive change.

Hakainde Hichilema, 
