"1578313020197093","BLANTYRE ADVENTIST HOSPITAL PRAISED FOR ADVANCING CARDIOLOGY SERVICES

Deputy Minister of Health, Hon. Noah Chimpeni-MP, commended Blantyre Adventist Hospital (BAH) and Hearts For Mission International (H4MI) for their dedication to advancing cardiology services in Malawi.

Speaking on Tuesday during a visit to BAH in Blantyre, Hon. Chimpeni praised the hospital's efforts in improving critical care and cardiac treatment. ""I would like to express my gratitude to Blantyre Adventist Hospital and Hearts For Mission International for their vision and commitment to enhancing cardiology and critical care services,"" he said.

The Deputy Minister noted that Malawi is privileged to host its fourth Cardiac and Open-Heart Surgery Camp, following the success of the previous three camps at BAH. Since the first camp in November 2023, a total of 52 patients have undergone life-changing surgeries.

Chimpeni stated that the government intends to support the initiative by reallocating funds previously used for referring patients abroad, ensuring the program's sustainability. BAH Chief Executive Officer, Mr. Kirby Kasinja, reaffirmed the hospital's commitment to working with the government to reduce the need for patients to seek treatment outside the country.

Meanwhile, H4MI CEO, Mr. Jason Blanchard, pledged to mobilize additional resources to expand access to these vital services.

