"1109606467991035","Sadly the orphaned elephant calf  which was moved from the Ugab herd did not make it despite the spirited  efforts by our Veterinary Officials to save its life even though the odds were against them.     

We wish to thank everyone that participated in this effort particularly the Elephant Human Relations Aid (EHRA), Ondjamba Hills, Okutala Etosha Lodge, Dr. Simone Hertzog and our passionate Veterinary Dr Janine Sharpe. Similarly we thank the members of the public for their concern and well wishes. We wish to take this opportunity to dispute and clarify assumptions that animals get more care that people. 

The Ministry has a very specific mandate given to it by the people of this country through a constitutional provision. Our mandate is driven from our National Constitution under Article 95 l and stipulates that Government will take steps to maintain Namibia's ecosystems, essential ecological processes and biological diversity for the benefit of current and future generations of Namibians. 

