"1138656428235891","The Ministry of Finance and Economic Affairs, through the Directorate of Public Finance Management successfully concluded the performance assessment exercise on Public Financial Management (PFM) Structures in public institutions held at the Atlantic Hotel from October 7th to 12th, 2024.
This exercise is crucial for evaluating the effectiveness and efficiency of our public institutions in managing financial resources. By systematically assessing PFM structures, we can identify strengths and areas for improvement, ensuring that public funds are utilized transparently and accountably. 
This not only fosters trust among citizens but also aligns our financial practices with national development goals. The collaborative nature of this assessment, involving various stakeholders, reinforces our commitment to enhancing governance and service delivery. 
