"1491475195196809","Dr. Swebby Macha Obstetrician & Gynaecologist consultant and Champion for AMPLI - PPHI project shares his insights on the WHO roadmap on Postpartum Hemorrhage (PPH) management at the on going Orientation meeting for Nurses and Midwives serving as Practicing Coordinators in Lusaka.

Postpartum Hemorrhage (PPH) is excessive bleeding after childbirth, If not managed properly, PPH can lead to severe complications, including shock and maternal death.
By following guidelines, healthcare professionals can reduce maternal mortality and improve outcomes for mothers worldwide.

Every mother deserves a safe pregnancy and childbirth. Let’s strengthen maternal health services.

