President Barrow said the Security have a responsibility to keep border communities safe.  However, in a bid to curb misconduct such as bribery at checkpoints, the President advised drivers to always have in possession of required documents to avoid providing an avenue to solicit bribes. He made the remarks while addressing a General Meeting held in Lamoi in Kantora District in the Upper River Region. 

On the other hand, President Barrow warned against the practice of traffic officers extorting money from motorists and drivers. He added that they have discovered some people disguised as security personnel around border villages luring money from drivers. He stressed to punish those who they find doing so, adding that his Government is committed to ensuring peace and stability in the country. 

During the meeting, the President presented a cheque for over 4 million Dalasi to 13 individuals under the GIRAV project. The beneficiaries are into poultry and vegetable production.

