"1268811195374853","We were deeply honored today to be guest of honor at this year's Builile Traditional Ceremony of the Bwile people, under the leadership of Senior Chief Puta VIII, Kasoma II, Tefwe Tefwe I.

The theme of the ceremony, ""Kabwile Ukaya Teka Bwile Ukabwela,"" beautifully reflects the land's richness and fertility, the abundance of natural resources, and the warm hospitality of the Bwile people.

Traditional ceremonies are vital in preserving our culture, as they represent our identity, guide our way of life, and instill a strong sense of self-respect.

We extend our heartfelt gratitude to the organizing committee and the Builile Royal Establishment for hosting such a vibrant and memorable event.

The government remains fully committed to ensuring food security for the people of Chienge. As part of this commitment, four new agricultural camps have been established, following the recruitment of agricultural extension officers to support our farmers.

With Luapula's abundant rainfall and healthy water bodies, the region has the potential to feed the entire nation. Our farmers should rise to this challenge. The government is committed to building more road infrastructure to ensure food can be efficiently delivered to markets.

Hakainde Hichilema,
