This evening, President Abdel Fattah El-Sisi received a phone call from U.S. President Joe Biden.

Spokesman for the Presidency, Ambassador Mohamed El-Shennawy, said the call focused on the vigorous mediation efforts led by Egypt, the United States and Qatar to achieve an agreement on a ceasefire in the Gaza Strip and an exchange of prisoners and detainees. President El-Sisi and the American President reviewed the latest progress in the relevant negotiations. They confirmed the crucial need for the concerned parties to commit to overcoming obstacles and demonstrate the required flexibility to reach an agreement.

President El-Sisi stressed the need to reach an immediate ceasefire agreement to put an end to the dire humanitarian suffering of citizens in the Strip, to allow humanitarian aid to enter without restrictions or obstacles, and to spare the region the consequences of expanding the scope of the conflict and the disastrous repercussions that may result.

