"1.26265E+15","Mrs Rookho Temil celebrates her 100th birthday

An official ceremony was held, yesterday at the Kailashnath Shivala Hall in Poudre D’Or Hamlet, to mark the 100th birthday of Mrs Rookho Temil. The event was organised by the Ministry of Social Integration, Social Security and National Solidarity in the presence of the Member of the National Assembly, Mr Sandeep Prayag, and other personalities.

On this special occasion Mrs Temil received a bouquet of flowers, a Centenarian Medal, a certificate, and a cheque amounting to Rs 26,203 from the Ministry. She was also presented with a hands-free telephone by Mauritius Telecom, while the Senior Citizens Council offered her a shield, a towel set, and a birthday card. In addition, the National Solidarity Fund remitted a cheque of Rs 10,000 to the centenarian.

Born on 3 November 1925 in La Laura, Saint Pierre, Mrs Temil is the daughter of Mr Kedar Luckmun, a labourer at l’Avenir Sugar Estate, and Mrs Beeptee Luckmun, a housewife. She was the fourth among nine siblings, all of whom have passed away.

The centenarian married Mr Sookhoo Temil at the age of 15 and later settled with him in Poudre D’Or Hamlet, where they were civilly married in 1953. In addition to managing her household, she cultivated sugarcane, reared livestock, and worked as a dressmaker until her 50s.

Known for her kindness and willingness to help others, she supported neighbours and relatives with advice, food, and financial aid. Her husband, a self-employed sugarcane grower, passed away in 1981 at the age of 59. The couple raised nine children and today she enjoys the company of 23 grandchildren and 28 great-grandchildren.

Mrs Temil enjoys watching television and listening to the radio. She speaks Creole, Bhojpuri, and Hindi, and is literate in Hindi. Her diet is mainly vegetarian, with a preference for light meals such as soup and purée. She credits her long life to her faith in God, compassion towards others, and the constant love and support of her family.","English","politics","domestic politics","not foreign politics","resource distribution","national government","specific locality or group","not applicable","Poudre D'Or Hamlet","resources for women","not applicable","no mention of the US","no mention of the Russia","no mention of the China","no mention of the UN","no mention of the IMF","no mention of democracy","not anti-western","national unity","subgroup unity","Poudre D'Or Hamlet community","no mention of africa","no mention of political opponents","religious","no mention of violent group","not specifically patriotic","SOCIAL WELFARE;CULTURE"
