"947557567765875","Minister of Gender, Community Development, and Social Welfare, Jean Sendeza, has expressed satisfaction with the transformation that has been registered in the lives of beneficiaries of the Social Cash Transfer Program (SCTP) in Blantyre.

Speaking during interaction with SCTP beneficiaries from  Traditional Authority Chigaru in the district on Friday,  Sendeza said it was pleasing to note that many of the beneficiaries, including the elderly, people with disabilities, and widows, invested their stipends in livestock production and other income-generating activities to support their families with food and income.

The minister also hailed the Blantyre District Council for using the electronic payment system instead of cash payment to transfer funds to the beneficiaries of the programme.

A widow, Virginia Ntapasha, said she bought livestock and supports her children with basic necessities using funds she receives through her TNM Mpamba mobile wallet. Another beneficiary, Harison Maluwa, said he operates a grocery shop on top of buying inputs for his maize field.

SCTP is a Malawi Government initiative under the Social Protection Programme. 
In Blantyre, the programme is supported by the World Bank, and it has 10,375 beneficiary households.","English","politics","domestic politics","not foreign politics","resource distribution","national government;international organisations","specific locality or group","not applicable","Traditional Authority Chigaru Blantyre district","resources for women","not applicable","no mention of the US","no mention of the Russia","no mention of the China","neutral towards the UN","no mention of the IMF","no mention of democracy","not anti-western","no mention of the nation or national unity","subgroup unity","elderly people with disabilities and widows in Traditional Authority Chigaru Blantyre district","no mention of africa","no mention of political opponents","no mention of religion","no mention of violent group","not specifically patriotic","SOCIAL WELFARE;ECONOMY;EDUCATION"
