"1285469999280196","I am delighted to share the details of a recent courtesy call with His Excellency Christopher Cooter, the High Commissioner of Canada, on 25th July 2024.

We are honoured to have welcomed H.E. Cooter back to Lesotho, and we appreciate his commitment to our Royal call for consultations with His Majesty the King.

Canada, a nation I had the pleasure of visiting a few years ago, has maintained warm and cordial diplomatic relations with Lesotho since our independence in 1966. Over the years, Canada has been a reliable partner, supporting us in health, housing, and human resource development through the Canadian International Development Agency (CIDA), and contributing to our education system via the Global Partnership for Education (GPE). Even during the COVID-19 crisis, Canada extended a helping hand to Lesotho.

We are grateful for this continued support and look forward to deepening our cooperation in strategic areas such as:
- Building agricultural productivity to reclaim Lesotho as the granary of Southern Africa
- Investing in renewable energies, recognising Lesotho as the water tower of the sub-region
- Developing infrastructure, especially road networks to connect the whole country

At the multilateral level, our two countries often collaborate naturally, sharing common values, principles, and aspirations for peace, development, and respect for human rights. This has facilitated Lesotho's support for Canadian requests for candidature.

We are now counting on Canada's support for Lesotho's candidate, Mr. Joshua Setipa, for the position of Secretary General of the Commonwealth at the upcoming election in Samoa this October. Mr. Setipa, endorsed by SADC, brings a wealth of experience from senior roles at the United Nations, the World Trade Organisation, the World Bank, and currently the Commonwealth Secretariat. It's worth noting that the principle of regional rotation should be observed, as the last African holder of this position was from West Africa. We hope Canada will consider these factors and support our candidate, while also mobilizing other members of the Commonwealth Family.

Thank you, H.E. Cooter, for taking the time to visit Lesotho. We understand you may soon be leaving your post, as we've received a request for accreditation of your successor. We wish you well in your future endeavours and hope you continue to champion Lesotho’s interests.

Thank you. 🇱🇸🇨🇦

