"1217659350349635","Inauguration of Village 25 Community Centre and a library in Agalega 

The Prime Minister, Minister of Defence, Home Affairs and External Communications, Minister for Rodrigues, Outer Islands and Territorial Integrity, Mr Pravind Kumar Jugnauth, inaugurated the Centre Communautaire Village 25 (Village 25 Community Centre) and the Bibliothèque du Nord, yesterday afternoon, in the North Island of Agalega, with a view to fostering social engagement, local talent and a reading culture.

The Prime Minister was accompanied by a Ministerial delegation, Members of Parliament, the High Commissioner of the Republic of India, Mrs K. Nandini Singla, and several other personalities. 

Following the unveiling of the commemorative plaque, Mr Jugnauth attended a cultural programme comprising, among others, an exhibition held in the premises of the community centre. Agaleans thus had the opportunity to showcase their culinary and handicraft talents. 

The key ingredient of the Agalean cuisine is coconut. ‘Seraz’, the traditional food peculiar to Agalega, is a rich coconut milk stew of fish, octopus and lentils. Other fish dishes also feature among the culinary specialties of the island. 

As for the handicrafts, they are fabricated using coconut, old clothing, broken umbrellas, bottles found on the beach, and shells. Recently, the inhabitants of Agalega, especially women from the ‘Fam Agalega’ Association, received training from a teacher from MEDCO Agalega to enhance their craft skills.

New Bibliothèque du Nord
A commemorative plaque for the library was unveiled, too, on the same occasion. The Indian High Commissioner, Mrs Singla, handed over books of various genres, in both English and French languages, to the Acting Resident Manager, Mr Emmanuel Jasmin, hence, adding to the 500 books provided from the Centre de Lecture et d’Animations Culturelles. 

The overarching objective of the setting up of this library is to instil a reading culture among people of different age groups, particularly among students, to improve their academic performance. Besides, the library is equipped with four computer sets, and Wi-Fi internet connection will be provided.

 

The first day visit and inaugural ceremony in Agalega concluded with singing and dancing performances by Agalean artists.","English","politics","domestic politics","foreign politics","resource distribution","national government;other state","specific locality or group","not applicable","Agalega North Island","resources for women","not applicable","no mention of the US","no mention of the Russia","no mention of the China","no mention of the UN","no mention of the IMF","no mention of democracy","not anti-western","national unity","subgroup unity","residents of Agalega North","no mention of africa","no mention of political opponents","no mention of religion","no mention of violent group","not specifically patriotic","CULTURE;EDUCATION;ENVIRONMENT"
