"717003824445873","♻️ Aujourd’hui, j’ai eu le plaisir de me rendre sur le site EcoTech, une initiative locale portée par trois jeunes Djiboutiens.  

Sur place, j’ai vu une réalité concrète, utile, et porteuse d’espoir : de la collecte au tri, jusqu’au recyclage, des équipes engagées transforment nos déchets plastiques en matières premières et donnent une seconde vie à ce qui polluait hier notre environnement. C’est un travail remarquable, sérieux, et profondément inspirant.

Cette dynamique s’inscrit pleinement dans l’ambition de long terme portée par Son Excellence M. Ismaïl Omar Guelleh, Président de la République de Djibouti, et dans notre cap national : Vision Djibouti 2035, qui appelle à une croissance durable, une économie modernisée et une trajectoire de développement plus responsable.   
Elle s’inscrit aussi dans l’esprit du Plan National de Développement 2025–2030, qui vise à accélérer la diversification et à renforcer la résilience de notre pays.  

Je veux saluer les équipes d’EcoTech et leurs partenaires qui font vivre cette chaîne au quotidien. Et j’adresse un remerciement particulier au Groupe Coubèche, dont le soutien constant démontre qu’innovation et responsabilité peuvent avancer ensemble.  

J’en appelle à tous les Djiboutiens : trions davantage, ramenons nos plastiques, recyclons. Chaque bouteille déposée est un geste simple, mais c’est aussi un acte de civisme, de fierté, et de protection de notre avenir commun. 

Ensemble, faisons du recyclage un réflexe national, pour un Djibouti plus propre, plus fort et plus durable.","French","politics","domestic politics","not foreign politics","not resource distribution","not applicable","not applicable","not applicable","not applicable","not applicable","mentions climate change","no mention of the US","no mention of the Russia","no mention of the China","no mention of the UN","no mention of the IMF","no mention of democracy","not anti-western","national unity","no mention of specific subgroup","not applicable","no mention of africa","no mention of political opponents","no mention of religion","no mention of violent group","patriotism","PUBLIC LANDS;ECONOMY;EDUCATION"
"1208549623623194","The President of Seychelles 🇸🇨, Mr Wavel Ramkalawan engaged in fruitful bilateral talks with his with his Cuban counterpart,🇨🇺 President Miguel Díaz-Canel Bermúdez earlier this evening.

President Ramkalawan is currently on an official visit in Cuba.

Havana, Cuba – 19 September: The President of the Republic of Seychelles, Wavel Ramkalawan, held official bilateral discussions with Cuban President Miguel Diaz-Canel Bermudez on Tuesday.

During the meeting, President Ramkalawan expressed his gratitude for the warm welcome extended to the Seychelles delegation and commended the strong diplomatic ties between the two island nations, which have spanned over four decades. Despite the geographic distance, he noted, the enduring relations between Seychelles and Cuba is rooted in shared values and mutual respect.

""Our present bilateral cooperation is both dynamic and evolving, and we anticipate continuous engagements on important global matters. I wish to reaffirm my personal commitment to work closely with you towards maintaining and consolidating the deep-seated relations that exists between Seychelles and Cuba.“ said President Ramkalawan.

President Diaz-Canel, in turn, thanked Seychelles for its consistent support of Cuba, particularly regarding the Cuban resolution against the U.S. embargo, and for President Ramkalawan’s participation in the G-77 and China Summit in Havana last year.

The two leaders agreed on key areas to further enhance cooperation, namely in the healthcare domain, pharmaceuticals, education and capacity building, cultural exchanges, as well as exploring new avenues of collaboration.

As part of the official visit, the two nations signed three bilateral agreements, enhancing collaboration in the areas of criminal justice, environmental protection, and academic-diplomatic training.

President Ramkalawan also paid tribute to Cuban national hero José Martí by laying a wreath at his monument, followed by a tour of the memorial.","English","politics","not domestic politics","foreign politics","not resource distribution","not applicable","not applicable","not applicable","not applicable","not applicable","mentions sustainability","negative towards the US","no mention of the Russia","neutral towards China","no mention of the UN","no mention of the IMF","no mention of democracy","anti-western","no mention of the nation or national unity","no mention of specific subgroup","not applicable","no mention of africa","no mention of political opponents","no mention of religion","no mention of violent group","not specifically patriotic","INTERNATIONAL AFFAIRS;HEALTH;EDUCATION"
