"806550671957389","Statement by His Excellency Dr Nangolo Mbumba, President of the Republic of Namibia, on the Occasion of the Launch of the Dr Hage G. Geingob Commemorative Bank Note

Ladies and Gentlemen, 

Good morning to you all.

The launch of the Dr. Hage Geingob commemorative bank note comes against the backdrop of the sudden passing of the Founding Father and First President of Namibia, Dr Sam Shafiishuna Nujoma on February 8 and subsequent burial on Saturday 1st March, 2025; thus, our hearts remain heavy with sorrow. Initially, we had planned the launch for February 10, but understandably, it had to be postponed to today. 

Director of Ceremonies,
Ladies and Gentlemen,

As the African proverb goes, ‘A tree is known by its fruit.’ Dr. Hage G. Geingob’s life and legacy are an enduring testament to the strength of character, vision, and leadership that Africa’s greatest sons have embodied. Dr. Geingob’s ability to transform challenges into opportunities, his profound belief in Pan-African solidarity and resilience, and his visionary understanding of our struggles and triumphs set him apart as a transformational African statesman. He was indeed a nation builder, who showed us that we can all live in peace and harmony as Namibians regardless of our regional, religious, tribal and economic differences.

Director of Ceremonies,
Ladies and Gentlemen,

This commemorative banknote cements Dr Geingob’s vision which was not only for economic recovery and growth but also for shared economic prosperity for all the Namibian citizens, in the spirit of his famous motto that “No One should feel left out from the Namibian House.” His leadership prioritized championing the diversification of our economy through ground-breaking initiatives in renewable energy, trade, and industrialization among others. Dr Geingob, through visionary leadership built bridges and developed networks to establish Namibia as a frontier for new economic initiatives and opportunities across our region, the continent and beyond, for the welfare of all our citizens. 

Director of Ceremonies,
Ladies and Gentlemen,

In celebration of Dr. Geingob’s remarkable life, we must also recognise those who stood by him throughout his journey. To his wife, Madame Monica Geingos, children and loved ones, we owe you profound gratitude. You shared him with the nation, often sacrificing precious moments so that he could serve Namibia, and for that, we honour you today for and for decades to come. Similarly, we extend our profound appreciation to the extended Geingob family both the paternal and maternal sides, and to his friends, comrades and colleagues for having enriched his life in many different ways.
 
This memorable occasion is made possible through the collaborative efforts of the Parliament and Namibia’s Central Bank, in commemoration of Namibia’s Constitution Day and recognition of 35 years of constitutional democracy by honouring Dr Geingob as one of the principal architects of our supreme law - the Constitution. 

In this vein, we pay tribute to the Members of the Constituent Assembly, both those who have gone before us as well as those still among us. These are the pioneers who worked tirelessly with Dr. Geingob to craft the very foundation of our democracy. Their wisdom, foresight, and commitment to justice, peace, democracy and stability ensured that Namibia’s Constitution became a globally respected document - one that has upheld peace, democracy, stability and the rule of law for over three decades. 

In conclusion, let us carry with us the spirit and values of our Third President Dr. Geingob – unity, transparency, inclusivity, and peace. Let us honour him by continuing to build the Namibian House which he so passionately envisioned.  May we always stand united in peace and stability as one people, One Namibia, One Nation. 

With these words, it is now my distinct pleasure to declare this commemorative bank note in honour of Dr Hage G. Geingob officially launched.

