"4122245544704961","His Excellency President Cyril Ramaphosa holds a bilateral meeting with His Excellency Prime Minister Andrew Holness of Jamaica on the margins of the G20 Leaders’ Summit, hosted by South Africa at the Johannesburg Expo Centre, Gauteng Province.

South Africa and Jamaica enjoy warm and longstanding relations, underpinned by the establishment of formal diplomatic ties on 09 September 1994 and marked by the celebration of the 30th Anniversary of Diplomatic Relations in September 2024. Bilateral cooperation is guided by the Memorandum of Understanding on Political Consultations signed in 2015, through which both countries continue to broaden engagement and strengthen ties across multiple sectors.

Political Consultations have reviewed progress in areas such as science and technology, sports, arts and culture, transport, trade and economic relations, and twinning agreements, while exploring new avenues of cooperation in agriculture, health and tourism. The two countries reaffirm their shared values of solidarity, human rights, democracy, sustainable development, respect for international law, and a steadfast commitment to multilateralism and the central role of the United Nations.

